    {
      "id": "claim_0d8574c6717049c2b9b514639210ae5f",
      "statement": "The wire formats are: SDP encoded via sdp-compact plus URL-safe substitutions (/ -> _, + -> ~, = -> -); offer link ?s=<offerSDP> plus optional i (STUN override, accepted only when in the STUN_SERVERS allowlist), c (chunk size, validated against CHUNK_SIZE_OPTIONS with 32 KB fallback), and p (base64 RSA public key, encryption only; a malformed key downgrades the session to plaintext with an error toast); answer code <encodedAnswerSDP>|<base64 RSA public key or empty>. sdpDecode throws synchronously on empty, invalid-base64, or non-SDP input, so both user-controllable decode sites (the s link param and the answer code) are guarded with try/catch and surface an error toast instead of crashing the page (PR #45).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/OfferPage.svelte#L43-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3bdd1ad599ab8a0f57235736ad7534adfd7c3b151028980895f2795a990f81cd:"
        },
